---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Back to nature | Aura Homes"
  description="Beautiful second-life rooms that bring people back to nature, one room at a time."
  descriptor="Back to nature"
>
  <main id="top">
    <section class="page-lead">
      <p class="story-kicker">Back to nature</p>
      <h1>Back outside.</h1>
      <p class="story-lede">Bring you back to nature, one beautiful room at a time.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="page-body">
      <p>A room at the edge of the grass. A desk that faces the meadow. A tub with the weather still in the air. The work is careful, and a little technical. The point is simpler than the work: more of the day spent where the light is real.</p>
      <p>The wifi can come. The meadow was already here.</p>
      <p>The room itself is on <a href="/rooms">Rooms</a>. The reason it stays low, and what comes after it, is the <a href="/story">story</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
